# Lazarus IDE-first UI

## Project stack

- **LazyCodingAgent** is a **Lazarus + LCL** desktop application (Free Pascal compiler under the hood).
- Default workflow: open `lazycodingagent.lpi` in the **Lazarus IDE**, edit forms and frames in the **Form Designer**, build with the IDE or `lazbuild`.
- **No Lazarus design package required:** stream **`TButton`** (and **`TPanel`** tab hosts) in form `.lfm` files; at runtime call **`EnsureThemedButton`** / **`Style*Button`** ([`fraThemedButton.pas`](fraThemedButton.pas)) and **`EnsureThemedTabHost`** ([`fraThemedTabs.pas`](fraThemedTabs.pas)). Open forms via the **`.pas`** file (F12), not a standalone `.lfm` tab.
- Do **not** nest `pbFace`, `pbTabs`, or `pnlPages` inside form `.lfm` files. Do **not** use `Parent = fra….pnlPages` in `.lfm` (unknown property). Do **not** stream `TThemedButtonFrame` / `TThemedTabHostFrame` on forms (IDE/Codetools without a package).
- Do **not** treat this repo as a console-only or “code-only UI” FPC project. Every visual surface must remain **editable in Lazarus** for layout.

## Lazarus IDE contract (hard requirements)

### Layout lives in `.lfm`

- **`TForm`** and **`TFrame`** subclasses use paired **`.pas` + `.lfm`**, `{$R *.lfm}`, designer **`published`** fields, and `inherited` in constructors where applicable.
- Use normal **`TForm.Create(Application)`** or **`Create(AOwner)`** for modal dialogs—not `CreateNew` + manual `BuildForm` for user-facing UI.
- **Geometry and hierarchy** belong in the **`.lfm`** (`Align`, `Anchors`, tab order, captions). The **`.pas`** file holds **published** components and **event handlers** wired from the `.lfm`, plus business logic in `private` / `implementation`.
- Do **not** build designer-owned layout with **`TXXX.Create(Self)`** + manual **`SetBounds`** / parent assignment for new UI. Use the palette on a form or frame instead.

### Standard LCL component palette only

- Use stock LCL controls from the component palette: `TForm`, `TFrame`, `TPanel`, `TLabel`, `TPageControl`, `TTabSheet`, `TMemo`, `TComboBox`, `TListBox`, `TSpeedButton`, `TSplitter`, `TMainMenu`, etc.
- **Actions and dialog buttons:** place **`TButton`** in the designer; in `ApplyTheme` / `FormCreate` call `StylePrimaryButton` / `StyleCancelButton` / `StyleDestructiveButton` from [fraThemedButton.pas](fraThemedButton.pas) (they upgrade to `TThemedButtonFrame` at runtime so dark/light palette matches on Qt5/Linux).
- Apply look-and-feel at runtime via [uTheme.pas](uTheme.pas)—not custom tab control subclasses.
- **Do not reintroduce** removed bespoke UI units: `uCustomTabControl`, `uDockPanel`, `uAppLogo`. Use [`fraThemedTabs.pas`](fraThemedTabs.pas) (`TThemedTabHostFrame`) for tab strips; host `TPanel`s + [uPanelDetach.pas](uPanelDetach.pas) for detach.

### Published events and designer wiring

- Declare **published** components and event methods on the form/frame class. Wire `OnCreate`, `OnClick`, `OnChange`, and similar in **`.lfm`** when the designer supports it.
- Any handler named in a `.lfm` must appear in the class **`published`** section (before `private`).

### Narrow exceptions (not templates for new UI)

- [uPanelDetach.pas](uPanelDetach.pas): minimal floating **`TForm`** shell (`CreateNew`) that reparents an existing host panel.
- [uTerminalPanel.pas](uTerminalPanel.pas): terminal embedding (specialized; still standard LCL inside).
- Non-visual code (engines, HTTP, `TProcess`, etc.) is unchanged.

## What we already migrated (follow this)

- Main window chrome and panel hosts on [mainunit.lfm](mainunit.lfm) / [mainunit.pas](mainunit.pas): `TPanel`, `TThemedButtonFrame`, `TThemedTabHostFrame`, navigation `TSpeedButton`s.
- Settings and dialogs as designer forms: `frmSettings`, `frmHelp`, `frmModelSearch`, `frmEditSavedModel`, `frmEditRule`, `frmWorkspaceRules`, `frmNewWorkspace`, `frmOpenMarkdown`, `frmSyntaxSchemes`, and similar `frm*.lfm` pairs.
- Detach flow: [uPanelDetach.pas](uPanelDetach.pas) instead of `uDockPanel`.
- Tabs: **`TThemedTabHostFrame`** from [fraThemedTabs.pas](fraThemedTabs.pas) — page bodies as `TPanel` children of `pnlPages`, registered in `FormCreate` (not `uCustomTabControl` or native tab headers for themed areas).
- Composer mode and model: **`TThemedPickerFrame`** from [fraThemedPicker.pas](fraThemedPicker.pas). The menu opens upward. Do not put a native `TComboBox` back on the composer footer (the list opens downward and is clipped at the bottom of the window).

References: [mainunit.pas](mainunit.pas) / [mainunit.lfm](mainunit.lfm), [frmSettings.pas](frmSettings.pas) / [frmSettings.lfm](frmSettings.lfm), [frmModelSearch.pas](frmModelSearch.pas) / [frmEditSavedModel.pas](frmEditSavedModel.pas).

## Migration debt (do not extend)

These units still construct UI in code and should move to **`TFrame` + `.lfm`** over time. **Do not add new code-built layout** here; when changing UI, prefer converting to a frame with `.lfm` in the same change. If migration is out of scope, limit edits to logic only.

- [uChatPanel.pas](uChatPanel.pas)
- [uNavigationPanel.pas](uNavigationPanel.pas)
- [uUtilityPlanTab.pas](uUtilityPlanTab.pas)
- [uUtilityExecutionDetailTab.pas](uUtilityExecutionDetailTab.pas)
- [uFileEditorTab.pas](uFileEditorTab.pas)
- [uFileMarkdownTab.pas](uFileMarkdownTab.pas)
- [uTerminalPanel.pas](uTerminalPanel.pas) (evaluate `TFrame` + `.lfm` vs. keeping as a documented exception when migrating)

Embedded panels on the main form should ultimately be **`TFrame`** instances placed on host `TPanel`s in **mainunit.lfm**, not `TPanel` subclasses that `Create` children in Pascal.

## Layout conventions

- See [`lazarus-lcl-layout.mdc`](lazarus-lcl-layout.mdc) for **ChangeBounds** / dual-layout rules (`Align` vs `SetBounds`, combos, tabs, detach).
- Prefer `Align`, `Anchors`, and `BevelOuter = bvNone` on panels—set in the **designer** (`.lfm`) where possible.
- Place **host `TPanel`s**, **`TFrame`s**, and standard LCL controls on the main form in the designer.

## Theming (dark and light)

- Do **not** hardcode theme colors or fonts in `.lfm` (e.g. `clGray`, fixed `Color`). Use designer-neutral defaults; runtime applies [uTheme.pas](uTheme.pas).
- On show and on theme toggle: `ApplyAllThemes` / `ApplyTheme`, `ThemePalette`, `ApplyControlTheme`, `TThemedTabHostFrame.ApplyTheme`, `TThemedButtonFrame.ApplyTheme`, `StylePrimaryButton` / `StyleCancelButton` / `StyleDestructiveButton`, `ConfigureThemedListBox`, `StyleComboBox` + `StyleComboBoxDrawItem`, `ApplyPlatformChrome`.

## When adding UI

1. Add or extend layout in the **Form or Frame Designer** (`.lfm`). For main-window areas, register the frame on a host panel in [mainunit.lfm](mainunit.lfm).
2. Use **standard palette** components only; wire events in `.lfm` and implement handlers in `.pas`.
3. Keep business logic in `.pas`; call theme helpers from `FormCreate` / `ApplyTheme`, not from fixed LFM colors.
4. After changes, verify **dark and light** via `View > Toggle Light / Dark Theme` on the main form and reopen dialogs.
